<!--
  Write / send: an envelope in flight, 28 degrees up, two motion lines behind it along its
  own axis with a clear gap so nothing touches. The designer's send was a diagonal arrow out
  of a box, which is the external-link glyph everywhere else on Android; a letter with a flap
  is mail and nothing else.

  Pigeonholes set: a sorting case and the cards that move through it. 24-unit viewport,
  2.2 stroke, round caps and joins, white and tinted where it is used. Plain paths only,
  every coordinate already in place, so nothing here is scaled or transformed at runtime.
-->
